Pope Leo XIV will meet privately with survivors of clerical sexual abuse during a four-day visit to France next month. On Friday, the Vatican published the itinerary for the 25–28 September trip – the first papal state visit to the country since Benedict XVI visited in 2008.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/a919bb62-34d9-11f1-8abb-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-A7D49ZR.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/a919bb62-34d9-11f1-8abb-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-A7D49ZR.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">065720b0-925b-11f1-98cd-15ecfd29aa41</guid><pubDate>Fri, 07 Aug 2026 13:31:16 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/a919bb62-34d9-11f1-8abb-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-A7D49ZR.jpg">AFP - HANDOUT</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>DR Congo hands first prisoners back to M23 rebels under peace deal</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/africa/20260807-dr-congo-hands-first-prisoners-back-to-m23-rebels-under-peace-deal</link><description>
